cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use JEVPFN, cite this software and the datasets and models used in your study."
type: software
title: "JEVPFN: Comparing text representations for tabular prediction"
authors:
  - family-names: Goethals
    given-names: Andreas
    affiliation: KU Leuven
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: https://github.com/andreasgoethals/JEVPFN
url: https://github.com/andreasgoethals/JEVPFN
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research software comparing task-conditioned decision features, frozen text
  embeddings, supervised target-aware E5 embeddings and native-text prediction
  systems on 18 selected MulTaBench datasets. Decision requests use fixed task
  definitions and row text without fitting to dataset labels. Decision and embedding
  comparisons share six tabular predictors and five outer cross-validation folds;
  supervised adaptation and fitted preprocessing remain within training partitions.
  The software retains predictions, feature provenance, timings and validation evidence.
keywords:
  - tabular prediction
  - decision models
  - text representations
  - text embeddings
  - target-aware representation learning
  - reproducible evaluation
  - MulTaBench
